<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>
  <!-- Fix13: GrimWorld 40,000 - Talons of the Emperor (grimworld.talonOfTheEmperor) gives the
       Custodes bike an engine sustainer referencing SoundDef "valkloop":
         1.6/Vehicles/Defs/ThingDefs_Vehicles/DawnEagleBike/GW_Tank_CustodesBikePawn.xml:58-64
       No SoundDef by that name exists anywhere in the load order - the mod never shipped it - so
       -> "Could not resolve cross-reference: No Verse.SoundDef named valkloop found to give to
       Vehicles.VehicleSustainerEventEntry`1[Vehicles.VehicleEventDef]".
       There is no sensible substitute to guess at (it was presumably a Valkyrie engine loop), so
       drop the whole <li>: the bike just runs without an engine sustainer, which is what already
       happens today except without the log error. Matched by its <value> rather than by position,
       so an upstream reorder can't make this hit the wrong entry. success=Always so it goes quiet
       if the mod ever ships the sound. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationRemove">
    <success>Always</success>
    <xpath>/Defs//soundSustainersOnEvent/li[value="valkloop"]</xpath>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
